From b9cfe33cc7ba42215edae69d3739517c60435d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Dinh <andrewd@openssl.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:00:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ssl/quic/quic_impl.c: fix deadlock rejecting pending
 connection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If a new pending connection callback (set
by SSL_CTX_set_new_pending_conn_cb()) returns 0,
port_new_handshake_layer() frees the new pending connection while
the engine lock is still held.  ossl_quic_free() then calls qctx_lock()
on that same lock, so the listener deadlocks.

Only run qc_cleanup() without taking a lock and exit early
when ossl_quic_free() is called on a pending connection that has
no channel: a connection like that has no shared resources to clean up.

Resolves: https://github.com/openssl/project/issues/2129
Link: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33664#discussion_r4560006747
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Reviewed-by: Bob Beck <beck@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Saša Nedvědický <sashan@openssl.org>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Fri Nov 20 18:34:32 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33744
(cherry picked from commit 3b7808c21b7f05307b9f6ebd617c3ba42d87652b)
---
 ssl/quic/quic_impl.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c b/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c
index 92f85f0..5134b4f 100644
--- a/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c
+++ b/ssl/quic/quic_impl.c
@@ -783,6 +783,16 @@ void ossl_quic_free(SSL *s)
         return;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * A pending connection whose channel has been detached is being discarded
+     * by the port. It has no shared resources to clean up, and the port lock
+     * may already be held by the caller.
+     */
+    if (!ctx.is_stream && ctx.qc->pending && ctx.qc->ch == NULL) {
+        qc_cleanup(ctx.qc, /*have_lock=*/0);
+        return;
+    }
+
     qctx_lock(&ctx);
 
     if (ctx.is_stream) {
-- 
2.53.0

